@startuml fig7-history
!include style.iuml
title Figure 7 (revises 2.2 Figure 7): Search, filter, and sort the history (FR 5.4 to 5.6; R6, R13)

actor User
participant ":HistoryFragment" as UI
participant ":HistoryViewModel" as VM
participant ":GroupRepository" as GR
participant ":UserRepository" as UR
participant ":TransactionRepository" as TR
participant ":HistoryFilter" as F
participant "db :\nFirebaseFirestore" as DB

User -> UI : open History tab\n<b>(also on every return, pull to refresh</b>\n<b>or live update, Figure 10)</b>
UI -> VM : load(groupId)
VM -> GR : <b>getGroup(groupId, cb)</b>
GR --> VM : <b>cb.onSuccess(group)</b>
VM -> UR : <b>getUsers(group.memberIds, cb)</b>
UR --> VM : <b>cb.onSuccess(users)</b>
VM --> UI : <b>members, users (LiveData)</b>
note right of VM
  NEW: members are loaded first, for the names
  on each row and the choices in the member filter
end note
VM -> TR : getTransactions(groupId, cb)
TR -> DB : get groups/{groupId}/transactions
DB --> TR : documents
TR --> VM : cb.onSuccess(transactions)
VM -> VM : all = transactions; <b>totalCount = all.size();</b>\n<b>applyQuery(query): the current query is kept</b>\n<b>(was query = HistoryQuery.defaults() on every load)</b>
VM -> F : apply(all, query)
F --> VM : newest first
VM --> UI : visible (LiveData)<b>, totalCount, a copy of the query</b>
UI --> User : expenses and settlements, settlements labeled "Settlement";\n<b>"You lent $X" / "You borrowed $X" on each row, "12 transactions"</b>
opt <b>some transactions involve former members (D9)</b>
  VM -> UR : <b>getUsers(missing, cb), where missing =</b>\n<b>FormerMembers.missingUserIds(transactions, known)</b>
  UR --> VM : <b>cb.onSuccess(users)</b>
  VM --> UI : <b>users, visible (LiveData): rows show their names</b>
end
loop each change to keyword, <b>Match case</b>, type, category, member, or sort order<b>, or Clear filters</b>
  User -> UI : type a keyword, pick a filter, or toggle the sort;\n<b>tap Match case or Clear filters</b>
  UI -> VM : setKeyword(keyword) / setTypeFilter(type) /\nsetCategoryFilter(category) / setMemberFilter(uid) /\n<b>toggleSortOrder() (was setSortOrder(o)) /</b>\n<b>setMatchCase(matchCase) / clearFilters()</b>
  VM -> VM : update query; applyQuery(next)
  note right of VM
    NEW (R6): a category filter matches expenses only;
    picking Settlements clears it, and picking a category
    clears Settlements. clearFilters() keeps the sort
    order and the Match case choice.
  end note
  VM -> F : apply(all, query)
  F -> F : keep transactions matching keyword and every filter<b>;</b>\n<b>the keyword ignores case unless Match case</b>\n<b>is on, then the case must match (R13)</b>
  F -> F : sort by createdAt\n(NEWEST_FIRST or OLDEST_FIRST)<b>;</b>\n<b>ties by date, then id</b>
  F --> VM : results
  VM --> UI : visible (LiveData)<b>, a copy of the query for the chips</b>\n<b>and the Clear filters button</b>
  alt results are empty
    UI --> User : <b>"Nothing matches", "Try a different keyword</b>\n<b>or clear the filters." (was an empty list)</b>
  else results found
    UI --> User : matching transactions<b>, "Showing 3 of 12"</b>\n<b>while a keyword or filter is on</b>
  end
end
note over VM, F
  Filtering runs on the list already loaded;
  no database call is made
end note
User -> UI : tap a transaction
UI --> User : open TransactionDetailActivity

legend bottom left
<b>Bold</b> messages and notes marked NEW or CHANGED are departures from Project 2.2; plain = unchanged.
endlegend
@enduml
